import GroupApproximation.Algebra.WreathLampPushforward

/-!
# Sections 37.4-37.5: the telescope tower and the kernel of its limit

Section 37 iterates the collapse through an entire ascending HNN telescope.  The
sites `X₀ = G/Γ₀` are pushed forward first to `X₁ = G/Γ₁`, then to `X₂`, and so
on, and the whole tower has a limit: the quotient `G/N` by the union
`N = ⋃ₙ Γₙ`.  The combinatorial heart of Section 37.5 -- equation (37.17) -- is
that nothing is lost in the passage to the limit.  A lamp configuration killed
by the limit pushforward is already killed at some finite stage of the tower, so
the limit kernel is the increasing union of the stage kernels and inherits every
property that is stable under increasing unions.

The reason is a finiteness one.  Two sites are merged in the limit exactly when
they are merged at some finite stage, so each of the relations generating the
limit kernel is already a relation of one finite stage.  Here that idea is
carried by the presentation of the pushforward kernel established in
`GroupApproximation.WreathLampPushforward.ker_pushHom`: the kernel is generated
by the same-fibre differences, and a same-fibre difference for the limit map is
a same-fibre difference for every large enough stage.  Since the stage kernels
increase along the tower, the subgroup they generate is their union, and an
element of the limit kernel lies in one of them rather than merely in a product
of several.

Three hypotheses carry the tower.  Refinement says that each stage's fibres are
contained in the limit's; monotonicity says that later stages only ever merge
more sites; and the limit condition says that every merge performed by the limit
is already performed by some stage.  From these we obtain the union description
of the limit kernel, its identification with the supremum of the stage kernels,
the abstract form of the radical half of Theorem 37.5 -- any subgroup containing
every stage kernel contains the limit kernel -- and the corresponding statements
one level up, inside the permutational wreath products, where the pushforward is
the identity on the acting group and the kernel therefore lives entirely in the
lamp subgroup.

The analytic input of Theorem 37.5, that each stage kernel really does land in
the MF radical, is deliberately left as a hypothesis: this file proves the tower
bookkeeping, not the collapse criterion that feeds it.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation

namespace WreathTelescope

open WreathLampPushforward

universe u v w z

variable {K : Type u} [CommGroup K] {X : Type v} {Y : ℕ → Type w} {Z : Type z}

/-! ## Refining one site partition by another -/

/-- If the fibres of `r` refine those of `r'`, then the pushforward along `r`
kills less than the pushforward along `r'`.  Every same-fibre difference for `r`
is a same-fibre difference for `r'`, and those differences generate the
kernels. -/
theorem ker_pushHom_le_of_refines {V : Type*} {W : Type*} (r : X → V) (r' : X → W)
    (h : ∀ x x' : X, r x = r x' → r' x = r' x') :
    (pushHom (K := K) r).ker ≤ (pushHom (K := K) r').ker := by
  classical
  rw [ker_pushHom]
  refine le_trans (Subgroup.closure_mono ?_) (fiberDiffs_le_ker r')
  rintro w ⟨x, x', k, hq, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨x, x', k, h x x' hq, rfl⟩

/-- **Section 37.5.**  The stage kernels of the telescope form an increasing
sequence: a later stage merges every pair of sites that an earlier one merges,
so its kernel is larger. -/
theorem ker_pushHom_mono (q : ∀ n : ℕ, X → Y n)
    (hmono : ∀ {n m : ℕ} (x x' : X), n ≤ m → q n x = q n x' → q m x = q m x')
    {n m : ℕ} (hnm : n ≤ m) :
    (pushHom (K := K) (q n)).ker ≤ (pushHom (K := K) (q m)).ker :=
  ker_pushHom_le_of_refines (q n) (q m) fun x x' hx => hmono x x' hnm hx

/-! ## The limit kernel -/

/-- **Section 37.5, equation (37.17).**  A configuration annihilated by the limit
pushforward is annihilated by a single finite stage of the telescope.

The forward direction splits in two.  The limit kernel is generated by the
same-fibre differences of the limit map, and each such difference already lives
in a stage kernel because the two sites it compares are merged at some finite
stage; hence the limit kernel is contained in the supremum of the stage kernels.
That supremum is the union of the stage kernels, because monotonicity makes the
family directed.  The converse direction is refinement alone. -/
theorem mem_ker_pushHom_limit (q : ∀ n : ℕ, X → Y n) (qinf : X → Z)
    (hrefine : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x x' : X), q n x = q n x' → qinf x = qinf x')
    (hmono : ∀ {n m : ℕ} (x x' : X), n ≤ m → q n x = q n x' → q m x = q m x')
    (hlimit : ∀ x x' : X, qinf x = qinf x' → ∃ n : ℕ, q n x = q n x')
    (f : Lamp K X) :
    f ∈ (pushHom (K := K) qinf).ker ↔ ∃ n : ℕ, f ∈ (pushHom (K := K) (q n)).ker := by
  classical
  constructor
  · intro hf
    -- Each generator of the limit kernel compares two sites merged in the limit,
    -- hence merged at some finite stage, where it is already a relation.
    have hle : (pushHom (K := K) qinf).ker
        ≤ ⨆ n : ℕ, (pushHom (K := K) (q n)).ker := by
      rw [ker_pushHom, Subgroup.closure_le]
      rintro w ⟨x, x', k, hq, rfl⟩
      obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hlimit x x' hq
      exact le_iSup (fun m : ℕ => (pushHom (K := K) (q m)).ker) n
        (fiberDiffs_le_ker (q n) (Subgroup.subset_closure ⟨x, x', k, hn, rfl⟩))
    -- Monotonicity makes the stage kernels directed, so their supremum is their
    -- union and membership is witnessed by a single stage.
    have hdir : Directed (· ≤ ·) fun n : ℕ => (pushHom (K := K) (q n)).ker :=
      fun i j => ⟨max i j,
        ker_pushHom_le_of_refines (q i) (q (max i j))
          (fun x x' hx => hmono x x' (le_max_left i j) hx),
        ker_pushHom_le_of_refines (q j) (q (max i j))
          (fun x x' hx => hmono x x' (le_max_right i j) hx)⟩
    exact (Subgroup.mem_iSup_of_directed hdir).mp (hle hf)
  · rintro ⟨n, hn⟩
    exact ker_pushHom_le_of_refines (q n) qinf (hrefine n) hn

/-- **Section 37.5, equation (37.17).**  The kernel of the limit pushforward is
the supremum -- by `mem_ker_pushHom_limit` in fact the increasing union -- of the
kernels of the finite stages of the telescope. -/
theorem ker_pushHom_limit (q : ∀ n : ℕ, X → Y n) (qinf : X → Z)
    (hrefine : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x x' : X), q n x = q n x' → qinf x = qinf x')
    (hmono : ∀ {n m : ℕ} (x x' : X), n ≤ m → q n x = q n x' → q m x = q m x')
    (hlimit : ∀ x x' : X, qinf x = qinf x' → ∃ n : ℕ, q n x = q n x') :
    (pushHom (K := K) qinf).ker = ⨆ n : ℕ, (pushHom (K := K) (q n)).ker := by
  refine le_antisymm (fun f hf => ?_) (iSup_le fun n => ?_)
  · obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := (mem_ker_pushHom_limit q qinf hrefine hmono hlimit f).mp hf
    exact le_iSup (fun m : ℕ => (pushHom (K := K) (q m)).ker) n hn
  · exact ker_pushHom_le_of_refines (q n) qinf (hrefine n)

/-- **Theorem 37.5, radical half, in abstract form.**  If every finite stage of
the telescope collapses into a subgroup `R`, then so does the limit.  The
analytic content -- that the stage kernels lie in the MF radical -- enters only
through the hypothesis `hstage`; what is proved here is that no further collapse
is needed at the limit. -/
theorem ker_pushHom_limit_le (R : Subgroup (Lamp K X)) (q : ∀ n : ℕ, X → Y n)
    (qinf : X → Z)
    (hrefine : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x x' : X), q n x = q n x' → qinf x = qinf x')
    (hmono : ∀ {n m : ℕ} (x x' : X), n ≤ m → q n x = q n x' → q m x = q m x')
    (hlimit : ∀ x x' : X, qinf x = qinf x' → ∃ n : ℕ, q n x = q n x')
    (hstage : ∀ n : ℕ, (pushHom (K := K) (q n)).ker ≤ R) :
    (pushHom (K := K) qinf).ker ≤ R := by
  rw [ker_pushHom_limit q qinf hrefine hmono hlimit]
  exact iSup_le hstage

/-! ## The tower inside the wreath products -/

section Wreath

variable {G : Type*} [Group G] [MulAction G X]

/-- The wreath-level pushforward is the identity on the acting group, so an
element of the wreath product dies exactly when its acting part is trivial and
its lamp part dies. -/
theorem mem_ker_pushWreath {W : Type*} [MulAction G W] {r : X → W}
    (hr : ∀ (g : G) (x : X), r (g • x) = g • r x) (w : Wreath K G X) :
    w ∈ (pushWreath (K := K) r hr).ker ↔
      w.right = 1 ∧ w.left ∈ (pushHom (K := K) r).ker := by
  constructor
  · intro hw
    have hone := MonoidHom.mem_ker.mp hw
    refine ⟨?_, MonoidHom.mem_ker.mpr ?_⟩
    · have h1 : (pushWreath (K := K) r hr w).right = (1 : Wreath K G W).right :=
        congrArg SemidirectProduct.right hone
      rwa [pushWreath_right, SemidirectProduct.one_right] at h1
    · have h2 : (pushWreath (K := K) r hr w).left = (1 : Wreath K G W).left :=
        congrArg SemidirectProduct.left hone
      rwa [pushWreath_left, SemidirectProduct.one_left] at h2
  · rintro ⟨hright, hleft⟩
    refine MonoidHom.mem_ker.mpr (SemidirectProduct.ext ?_ ?_)
    · rw [pushWreath_left, SemidirectProduct.one_left]
      exact MonoidHom.mem_ker.mp hleft
    · rw [pushWreath_right, SemidirectProduct.one_right]
      exact hright

/-- The kernel of the wreath-level pushforward is the kernel of the lamp
pushforward, embedded by `SemidirectProduct.inl`. -/
theorem ker_pushWreath {W : Type*} [MulAction G W] (r : X → W)
    (hr : ∀ (g : G) (x : X), r (g • x) = g • r x) :
    (pushWreath (K := K) r hr).ker
      = ((pushHom (K := K) r).ker).map SemidirectProduct.inl := by
  ext w
  rw [mem_ker_pushWreath, Subgroup.mem_map]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hright, hleft⟩
    exact ⟨w.left, hleft, SemidirectProduct.ext (SemidirectProduct.left_inl _)
      ((SemidirectProduct.right_inl _).trans hright.symm)⟩
  · rintro ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨SemidirectProduct.right_inl f, by rwa [SemidirectProduct.left_inl]⟩

/-- **Sections 37.4-37.5 inside the wreath products.**  The kernel of the limit
map `Φ_∞` of (37.13) is the supremum of the kernels of the finite stages `Φ_n`
of the telescope. -/
theorem ker_pushWreath_limit [∀ n : ℕ, MulAction G (Y n)] [MulAction G Z]
    (q : ∀ n : ℕ, X → Y n) (qinf : X → Z)
    (hq : ∀ (n : ℕ) (g : G) (x : X), q n (g • x) = g • q n x)
    (hqinf : ∀ (g : G) (x : X), qinf (g • x) = g • qinf x)
    (hrefine : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x x' : X), q n x = q n x' → qinf x = qinf x')
    (hmono : ∀ {n m : ℕ} (x x' : X), n ≤ m → q n x = q n x' → q m x = q m x')
    (hlimit : ∀ x x' : X, qinf x = qinf x' → ∃ n : ℕ, q n x = q n x') :
    (pushWreath (K := K) qinf hqinf).ker
      = ⨆ n : ℕ, (pushWreath (K := K) (q n) (hq n)).ker := by
  rw [ker_pushWreath, ker_pushHom_limit q qinf hrefine hmono hlimit,
    Subgroup.map_iSup]
  exact iSup_congr fun n => (ker_pushWreath (q n) (hq n)).symm

/-- **Theorem 37.5, radical half, at the wreath level.**  A subgroup of the
wreath product containing every stage kernel contains the kernel of the limit
map. -/
theorem ker_pushWreath_limit_le [∀ n : ℕ, MulAction G (Y n)] [MulAction G Z]
    (R : Subgroup (Wreath K G X)) (q : ∀ n : ℕ, X → Y n) (qinf : X → Z)
    (hq : ∀ (n : ℕ) (g : G) (x : X), q n (g • x) = g • q n x)
    (hqinf : ∀ (g : G) (x : X), qinf (g • x) = g • qinf x)
    (hrefine : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x x' : X), q n x = q n x' → qinf x = qinf x')
    (hmono : ∀ {n m : ℕ} (x x' : X), n ≤ m → q n x = q n x' → q m x = q m x')
    (hlimit : ∀ x x' : X, qinf x = qinf x' → ∃ n : ℕ, q n x = q n x')
    (hstage : ∀ n : ℕ, (pushWreath (K := K) (q n) (hq n)).ker ≤ R) :
    (pushWreath (K := K) qinf hqinf).ker ≤ R := by
  rw [ker_pushWreath_limit q qinf hq hqinf hrefine hmono hlimit]
  exact iSup_le hstage

end Wreath

end WreathTelescope

end GroupApproximation
